{"created": "2026-08-30T00:45:49.357811+00:00", "modified": "2026-08-30T00:52:44.863765+00:00", "id": 22167512, "conceptrecid": "22151304", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22167512", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22151304", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22167512", "metadata": {"title": "Immunisation coverage and surveillance indicators preceding the 2026 measles outbreak in Bangladesh: data and code", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22167512", "publication_date": "2026-08-30", "description": "<p>Data and analysis code for a retrospective analysis of Bangladesh's routinely reported immunisation coverage, supplementary immunisation activity records, and monthly measles surveillance, 2012-2026. All data derived from public World Health Organization repositories (WIISE API, WUENIC 2025 revision, provisional monthly measles and rubella dataset), retrieved 26-28 August 2026. Includes numerator/denominator decomposition of reported coverage change, cohort susceptibility reconstruction, and comparison with six neighbouring countries. No individual-level data.</p>\n<p>Version 1.1.0 revises the cohort susceptibility model to include transplacental antibody and age-eligibility terms, and expands sensitivity analyses from three to seven. All six load-bearing coverage figures were independently re-verified against the WHO API on 28 August 2026. Susceptibility estimates in version 1.0.0 are superseded.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Sikder, Pranta", "affiliation": "The University of Texas at El Paso", "orcid": "0009-0000-8569-2541"}], "keywords": ["measles", "Bangladesh", "immunisation coverage", "vaccination", "disease surveillance", "health information systems"], "dates": [{"type": "collected", "description": "WHO data retrieval window", "start": "2026-08-26", "end": "2026-08-28"}], "version": "1.1.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"